1
00:00:14,120 --> 00:00:18,420
Aiming for the sunset
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:23,560
I kicked a pebble and my shoe flew off too.

3
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:29,240
Joking around,
right on the head of the gym teacher,

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,800
they laughed at me for staying so energetic.

5
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:36,140
Somewhere, a bit of good energy,

6
00:00:36,140 --> 00:00:38,680
as a sound too, it's something real.

7
00:00:38,680 --> 00:00:41,940
One nightmare, the unchanging streets

8
00:00:41,940 --> 00:00:43,880
are kinder than ever.

9
00:00:44,680 --> 00:00:46,880
Because the crows are calling,

10
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:48,720
the sun has already set.

11
00:00:49,680 --> 00:00:53,880
Are the yakitori stalls really there?

12
00:00:54,920 --> 00:00:57,460
Of the pointed hat,

13
00:00:57,460 --> 00:01:02,600
from the water pipes,
loud and big, the water pipes.

14
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:04,080
The sunset falls.

15
00:01:07,060 --> 00:01:10,060
Tomorrow it'll end with another drop

16
00:01:10,060 --> 00:01:12,720
Putting out a magazine again,
saying we're happy.

17
00:01:12,720 --> 00:01:14,640
Only after losing it did I realize.

18
00:01:14,640 --> 00:01:16,300
Because I'm a fool.

19
00:01:17,060 --> 00:01:17,620
Yeah

20
00:01:25,980 --> 00:01:27,220
Cherry blossom trouble!

21
00:01:30,960 --> 00:01:31,960
What did you say?

22
00:01:32,440 --> 00:01:36,200
That we still haven't secured a cherry
blossom viewing spot this late in the season?

23
00:01:36,200 --> 00:01:38,000
What's the meaning of this?

24
00:01:39,120 --> 00:01:41,040
Even if you ask what the meaning is,

25
00:01:41,500 --> 00:01:43,400
cherry blossom viewing
is still quite a way off,

26
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:46,020
so there's no need to
claim a spot this early.

27
00:01:47,680 --> 00:01:48,700
You're far too naive.

28
00:01:48,700 --> 00:01:51,800
Cherry blossom viewing is the
biggest spring event of all!

29
00:01:51,800 --> 00:01:53,100
If the viewing spot is

30
00:01:53,760 --> 00:01:54,980
next to a garbage dump,

31
00:01:54,980 --> 00:01:56,860
or near the toilets,

32
00:01:57,300 --> 00:01:59,620
or in a place with heavy foot traffic,

33
00:01:59,620 --> 00:02:02,420
or if some shady shop is nearby,

34
00:02:02,420 --> 00:02:04,380
you won't be able to enjoy
the cherry blossoms properly,

35
00:02:04,380 --> 00:02:07,700
and everyone who came
will be scarred for life.

36
00:02:08,480 --> 00:02:09,980
W-what, that's a bit over the top!

37
00:02:10,560 --> 00:02:12,260
It's not over the top at all!

38
00:02:12,260 --> 00:02:14,800
The premium spots where you can
truly enjoy the cherry blossoms

39
00:02:14,800 --> 00:02:16,120
are only a precious few.

40
00:02:17,620 --> 00:02:18,747
In the case of Ueno Park,

41
00:02:18,797 --> 00:02:21,740
the prime hanami spot is
one tennis court in size!

42
00:02:21,880 --> 00:02:23,720
That's all?

43
00:02:24,460 --> 00:02:28,103
Yes. That's why, Chief,
if we don't go reserve the spot right now,

44
00:02:28,153 --> 00:02:30,080
do you know what will happen!

45
00:02:30,480 --> 00:02:32,355
A-all right.

46
00:02:32,405 --> 00:02:35,400
I'll leave this matter entirely to Ryotsu.

47
00:02:36,860 --> 00:02:38,054
That's how it is.

48
00:02:38,104 --> 00:02:41,060
I want all of you to head
straight out to reserve the spot.

49
00:02:41,960 --> 00:02:43,200
What about our work?

50
00:02:43,640 --> 00:02:45,480
Of course, you'll manage both.

51
00:02:46,700 --> 00:02:48,400
We'll run out of time to play.

52
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:50,180
That's the same as a night shift.

53
00:02:51,140 --> 00:02:52,440
Don't talk back.

54
00:02:52,940 --> 00:02:54,360
This is an order.

55
00:02:55,100 --> 00:02:57,880
I've done spot-holding before,
back when I was a student.

56
00:02:57,880 --> 00:02:59,740
The day before is plenty.

57
00:02:59,740 --> 00:03:00,800
Yeah, exactly.

58
00:03:00,800 --> 00:03:02,640
Starting now would be way too early, right?

59
00:03:04,020 --> 00:03:06,620
If you're going to say that much,
I'll put you to the test.

60
00:03:07,120 --> 00:03:07,920
Test us?

61
00:03:08,660 --> 00:03:12,360
Within Ueno Park there are spots that
could be called the prime of the prime,

62
00:03:12,360 --> 00:03:14,340
and there are three super-prime spots.

63
00:03:15,480 --> 00:03:17,160
If you can hold one of them
until tomorrow's showdown,

64
00:03:17,160 --> 00:03:19,420
I'll admit you're right.

65
00:03:19,420 --> 00:03:20,280
Really?

66
00:03:20,280 --> 00:03:22,780
But if you fail,

67
00:03:22,780 --> 00:03:25,060
you'll follow my orders.

68
00:03:25,060 --> 00:03:25,820
Understood?

69
00:03:32,460 --> 00:03:33,500
One down!

70
00:03:34,060 --> 00:03:35,120
Next one's here

71
00:03:35,600 --> 00:03:36,680
This one's the last.

72
00:03:36,680 --> 00:03:38,180
Two down!

73
00:03:38,180 --> 00:03:39,800
Three down!

74
00:03:41,800 --> 00:03:43,400
So this is what Senior
Ryotsu was talking about.

75
00:03:43,400 --> 00:03:46,260
We've secured all three super-prime spots.

76
00:03:47,220 --> 00:03:48,240
Piece of cake.

77
00:03:48,880 --> 00:03:52,600
All that's left is to take turns
keeping watch until noon tomorrow.

78
00:03:56,580 --> 00:03:57,740
You fools.

79
00:03:58,200 --> 00:04:02,020
If you think laying down a tarp is enough to claim a spot,
you're dead wrong.

80
00:04:02,020 --> 00:04:04,260
The harsh reality of
reserving a cherry blossom spot.

81
00:04:04,660 --> 00:04:06,760
I'll teach you thoroughly.

82
00:04:13,360 --> 00:04:15,040
Wow, wow, wow, wow!

83
00:04:15,040 --> 00:04:16,340
Shift change!

84
00:04:20,900 --> 00:04:23,020
It should be Imai's turn next, right?

85
00:04:23,020 --> 00:04:26,040
Imai said he couldn't make
it because of an urgent job,

86
00:04:26,040 --> 00:04:30,160
I'm his high school friend,
and I was asked to fill in for him.

87
00:04:30,580 --> 00:04:31,300
I see.

88
00:04:33,060 --> 00:04:34,400
Well, then, the rest is up to you.

89
00:04:35,100 --> 00:04:36,480
Yes, leave it to me.

90
00:04:37,020 --> 00:04:37,660
Whoa...

91
00:04:39,620 --> 00:04:40,120
Hmph.

92
00:04:42,020 --> 00:04:43,040
No good

93
00:04:43,400 --> 00:04:46,120
Don't take a stranger's word at face value.

94
00:04:48,580 --> 00:04:49,860
Okay, your turn.

95
00:04:51,880 --> 00:04:53,020
What'd you just say, punk?

96
00:04:53,020 --> 00:04:53,720
You wanna go?

97
00:05:00,120 --> 00:05:02,700
I've always hated your Mario, you know.

98
00:05:03,920 --> 00:05:06,740
Your under-eye bags are creepier.

99
00:05:08,420 --> 00:05:09,200
Is this a fight?

100
00:05:09,200 --> 00:05:10,700
Looks like it.

101
00:05:13,560 --> 00:05:14,600
Aaaah!

102
00:05:14,600 --> 00:05:16,140
You bastard!

103
00:05:16,140 --> 00:05:18,540
Aaaah!

104
00:05:27,920 --> 00:05:30,160
Can't even touch a real woman,

105
00:05:30,160 --> 00:05:32,980
You're one to talk, you've been
piling up since the game started.

106
00:05:32,980 --> 00:06:00,900
Yeaaaaaaah!

107
00:06:05,740 --> 00:06:06,560
Here too.

108
00:06:07,840 --> 00:06:08,720
Kawashima!

109
00:06:13,480 --> 00:06:14,360
What happened?

110
00:06:20,360 --> 00:06:21,500
We got hit.

111
00:06:22,660 --> 00:06:23,440
That's a dirty trick!

112
00:06:23,440 --> 00:06:25,900
Your tarp was already spread out
all the way over there, though.

113
00:06:25,900 --> 00:06:26,880
Don't know.

114
00:06:26,880 --> 00:06:29,900
When I got here, there was nothing laid out!

115
00:06:31,180 --> 00:06:33,300
Maybe the wind blew it up?

116
00:06:33,760 --> 00:06:35,720
There's no wind blowing at all, you know.

117
00:06:38,940 --> 00:06:41,120
With this, all the super-prime spots

118
00:06:41,120 --> 00:06:42,860
are ours, then.

119
00:06:43,500 --> 00:06:45,400
Damn, we got hit.

120
00:06:45,960 --> 00:06:48,600
Now you know how tough reserving a spot is

121
00:06:49,160 --> 00:06:49,560
Yes.

122
00:06:50,500 --> 00:06:53,960
Listen, when reserving a spot,
never let your guard down.

123
00:06:53,960 --> 00:06:57,460
Even right now,
there are people eyeing the prime spots.

124
00:06:58,380 --> 00:06:59,180
Like that one -

125
00:07:02,020 --> 00:07:05,440
Come out!
You've been spying on us this whole time!

126
00:07:06,300 --> 00:07:09,660
As expected of Mister Ryotsu,
you noticed us after all.

127
00:07:10,220 --> 00:07:11,420
Who the hell are you?

128
00:07:11,420 --> 00:07:15,480
True, we are trying to secure a
spot for cherry blossom viewing.

129
00:07:15,900 --> 00:07:17,940
But it's not for these cherry blossoms.

130
00:07:18,540 --> 00:07:22,320
What? These guys are with the US government!

131
00:07:23,300 --> 00:07:25,300
They're said to be close
aides to the Vice President.

132
00:07:26,380 --> 00:07:30,760
The Vice President is a big Japan fan
and knows a lot about cherry blossoms too.

133
00:07:30,760 --> 00:07:34,940
He is very eager to hold a
hanami under the Mannen-zakura.

134
00:07:34,940 --> 00:07:36,500
Mannen-zakura.

135
00:07:36,500 --> 00:07:40,200
It's a legendary cherry tree
that almost no one knows about.

136
00:07:40,200 --> 00:07:44,500
It reaches full bloom much earlier than
other cherry trees start to blossom.

137
00:07:44,500 --> 00:07:48,520
It keeps its flowers for a while even
after the other cherry trees have scattered.

138
00:07:48,520 --> 00:07:53,040
So it apparently gives the impression
that it blooms all year round.

139
00:07:53,040 --> 00:07:58,200
Surveys over the past few years have revealed
that it apparently exists in the Okutama region.

140
00:07:58,640 --> 00:08:03,000
But the Vice President's schedule for
his visit to Japan is still unclear.

141
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:09,200
So I want you to secure a prime hanami spot so we're ready whenever we go,
Mister Ryotsu.

142
00:08:09,760 --> 00:08:10,560
What?!

143
00:08:11,620 --> 00:08:14,220
This is a request from
the Japanese government.

144
00:08:15,020 --> 00:08:15,820
The Japanese government.

145
00:08:16,600 --> 00:08:20,000
Of course, that means we'll be
getting paid for this, right?

146
00:08:20,780 --> 00:08:21,820
Of course.

147
00:08:23,460 --> 00:08:25,180
Leave it to me.

148
00:08:25,180 --> 00:08:29,220
Let's strengthen Japan-US friendship
through cherry blossom viewing.

149
00:08:30,080 --> 00:08:31,380
Thank you!

150
00:08:31,780 --> 00:08:32,140
Thank you very much.

151
00:08:34,380 --> 00:08:37,340
Damn it, we could get there
fast if we used a helicopter.

152
00:08:37,340 --> 00:08:41,180
We've been told not to use helicopters
because they'll scatter the blossoms.

153
00:08:41,180 --> 00:08:42,900
A little wind wouldn't hurt, would it?

154
00:08:52,500 --> 00:08:54,700
From here on, it's on foot

155
00:08:57,460 --> 00:08:58,600
There's a shop.

156
00:09:02,500 --> 00:09:03,480
Excuse us.

157
00:09:03,480 --> 00:09:04,960
Welcome.

158
00:09:05,520 --> 00:09:06,800
We'd like to ask you something.

159
00:09:06,800 --> 00:09:10,420
How long does it take from here
to get to the Mannen-zakura?

160
00:09:10,580 --> 00:09:11,760
Mannen-zakura?

161
00:09:11,960 --> 00:09:13,060
What's that?

162
00:09:13,900 --> 00:09:17,840
It's supposed to be a legendary cherry tree,
so even the locals might not know it.

163
00:09:17,840 --> 00:09:18,360
Yeah.

164
00:09:19,300 --> 00:09:24,660
There's nothing up there. I'm not saying this to be mean,
but you should turn back.

165
00:09:26,400 --> 00:09:27,800
Got it, got it.

166
00:09:29,440 --> 00:09:30,580
Hey there!

167
00:09:30,580 --> 00:09:32,760
Uggh.

168
00:09:37,340 --> 00:09:38,000
Whoa!

169
00:09:38,860 --> 00:09:41,120
The path is gone.

170
00:09:41,120 --> 00:09:43,140
Isn't there another way?

171
00:09:43,140 --> 00:09:45,420
Yeah, this is the only one.

172
00:09:45,420 --> 00:09:47,220
Looks like we have no
choice but to turn back.

173
00:09:47,220 --> 00:09:48,640
Can't be helped.

174
00:09:48,640 --> 00:09:50,000
Senpai.

175
00:09:50,860 --> 00:09:55,040
We get paid just to save a spot for hanami!

176
00:09:56,360 --> 00:09:58,940
Are we really going to
turn back over this much?

177
00:09:58,940 --> 00:10:02,540
Knew you'd say that. I guess we have no
choice but to keep going along with you.

178
00:10:04,040 --> 00:10:06,440
The bridge is gone.

179
00:10:06,440 --> 00:10:06,740
There's one!

180
00:10:10,200 --> 00:10:15,460
Come on, even we have to turn back here.
It's a bolo rope!

181
00:10:50,860 --> 00:10:52,600
Hey, can I go to my limit too?

182
00:10:52,600 --> 00:10:55,680
Hey, go on ahead, Ryotsu.

183
00:10:55,680 --> 00:10:56,610
What's wrong?

184
00:10:56,660 --> 00:10:59,800
Hang in there!
The Mannen-zakura is just ahead!

185
00:11:17,480 --> 00:11:19,680
So this is the Mannen-zakura.

186
00:11:38,440 --> 00:11:39,320
It's beautiful.

187
00:11:39,840 --> 00:11:42,120
I've never seen such
magnificent cherry blossoms.

188
00:11:42,740 --> 00:11:46,220
But I don't think anyone would
bother coming all the way out here.

189
00:11:46,220 --> 00:11:48,380
Is there even any point in reserving a spot?

190
00:11:48,380 --> 00:11:50,231
Whether there's a point or not,

191
00:11:50,281 --> 00:11:53,060
we get paid for reserving a spot here.

192
00:11:53,580 --> 00:11:56,320
Let's enjoy ourselves until
the Vice President gets here.

193
00:11:57,860 --> 00:12:00,495
Hoo-ray, yai yai, yai yai!

194
00:12:00,545 --> 00:12:03,040
Ko-ra, sorya sorya sorya!

195
00:12:03,040 --> 00:12:05,274
Hand's out, hand's out!

196
00:12:05,324 --> 00:12:07,380
Hand's out, sotto!

197
00:12:07,840 --> 00:12:11,240
Hai-raa, hai-raa, hai-raa!

198
00:12:13,360 --> 00:12:17,180
Aaaaaaah!

199
00:12:24,340 --> 00:12:25,740
Mm...

200
00:12:27,520 --> 00:12:28,920
Mm...

201
00:12:34,920 --> 00:12:36,380
Guess I'll take a leak.

202
00:12:36,380 --> 00:12:37,060
Oof.

203
00:12:40,360 --> 00:12:41,320
Wh-what?

204
00:12:53,460 --> 00:12:55,200
What's wrong, Ryo-san?

205
00:12:55,200 --> 00:12:57,000
It's refreshing this early in the morning.

206
00:12:57,000 --> 00:13:00,140
You guys, look around you. Look around!

207
00:13:03,360 --> 00:13:05,220
How did we end up somewhere like this?

208
00:13:06,260 --> 00:13:07,720
What the hell is going on here?

209
00:13:21,080 --> 00:13:21,800
Animation

210
00:13:23,680 --> 00:13:24,960
When did this get here?

211
00:13:24,960 --> 00:13:26,400
Don't just barge in like that!

212
00:13:28,240 --> 00:13:30,380
I reserved this spot!

213
00:13:30,380 --> 00:13:32,840
You're the old man from the general
store at the foot of the mountain!

214
00:13:32,840 --> 00:13:35,480
You said you didn't know
anything about Mannen-zakura!

215
00:13:35,480 --> 00:13:36,800
So you were lying!

216
00:13:36,800 --> 00:13:40,840
We struggled so hard just to get here,
so how did you...

217
00:13:41,380 --> 00:13:44,500
Heh heh,
I know a back path that no one else knows!

218
00:13:44,500 --> 00:13:49,460
So you're the one who blocked
the path and dropped the bridge!

219
00:13:49,460 --> 00:13:53,040
I won't let you hold a hanami here.
Absolutely not!

220
00:13:53,040 --> 00:13:54,860
Who the hell are you?

221
00:13:54,860 --> 00:13:56,860
Heh.

222
00:13:56,860 --> 00:14:01,960
The romantic scent of cherry blossoms...
I've loved them for so many years.

223
00:14:01,960 --> 00:14:04,020
President of the Mannen-zakura
Preservation Society.

224
00:14:06,520 --> 00:14:28,240
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

225
00:14:28,240 --> 00:14:32,160
People will start climbing the
trees and snapping the branches!

226
00:14:32,900 --> 00:14:35,620
If you stay there,
Mannen-zakura is finished!

227
00:14:36,200 --> 00:14:39,660
It won't come to that!
I've blocked every path leading here!

228
00:14:40,380 --> 00:14:41,100
That's it!

229
00:14:43,700 --> 00:14:45,460
Cherry Blossom Maze Jutsu!

230
00:14:46,400 --> 00:14:47,840
Don't mess with us!

231
00:14:48,160 --> 00:14:51,600
You're the one who moved us to that place,
aren't you?

232
00:14:51,980 --> 00:14:54,840
We're here on the government's request,
you know.

233
00:14:55,920 --> 00:14:58,960
That's right! If we don't let the
US Vice President enjoy hanami here,

234
00:14:58,960 --> 00:15:01,460
US-Japan relations could be damaged,
you know.

235
00:15:03,080 --> 00:15:07,420
Now that I've heard that,
I can't hand over this spot at all.

236
00:15:07,900 --> 00:15:08,560
What did you say?

237
00:15:08,880 --> 00:15:12,020
If it becomes known that the
US Vice President held a hanami,

238
00:15:12,380 --> 00:15:15,440
hanami crowds will flood
in from all over the world!

239
00:15:16,580 --> 00:15:17,300
What?

240
00:15:18,100 --> 00:15:18,460
Who?

241
00:15:27,120 --> 00:15:32,100
Aaaah! Cray,
this is the real cherry blossom storm!

242
00:15:32,760 --> 00:15:33,280
Me

243
00:15:37,020 --> 00:16:04,060
Grrrrrrrrrrrrrr...

244
00:16:05,280 --> 00:16:06,020
I'll give it back to you!

245
00:16:14,020 --> 00:16:16,420
That spot is my place!

246
00:16:21,440 --> 00:16:24,760
You're impressed This is the master
of the cherry blossom electric guitar!

247
00:16:29,660 --> 00:16:31,180
Don't you dare come back!

248
00:16:33,420 --> 00:16:34,654
Damn it...

249
00:16:34,704 --> 00:16:38,300
Do you think I'd give up over this?

250
00:16:49,880 --> 00:16:50,740
He's asleep.

251
00:16:50,740 --> 00:16:51,340
Yeah.

252
00:16:51,340 --> 00:16:54,940
He's just one man.
There's bound to be an opening.

253
00:16:55,480 --> 00:16:57,380
Okay... here we go.

254
00:16:57,380 --> 00:16:59,400
Okay... okay...

255
00:16:59,740 --> 00:17:00,400
Well...

256
00:17:03,300 --> 00:17:04,660
He's noticed us!

257
00:17:04,660 --> 00:17:05,880
Charge!

258
00:17:05,880 --> 00:17:07,040
Do it!

259
00:17:07,040 --> 00:17:09,380
You incorrigible old fool!

260
00:17:09,380 --> 00:17:11,180
Cherry Blossom Storm Technique!

261
00:17:23,040 --> 00:17:26,000
Damn it!
Then it's the Cherry Blossom Electric Jutsu!

262
00:17:27,100 --> 00:17:31,040
Idiot! Thick rubber gloves
won't let electricity through!

263
00:17:35,360 --> 00:17:36,740
